<p>(1) Due to the sale of the direct sales offices on May 31, 1996, the income statement for the three and six-month periods ended June 30, 1996 includes the revenue and the related operating profit for the direct offices through the date of sale.</p>
<p>The company said the 1996 second quarter results included two months of revenue from the direct sales and service organization and network business, and a pretax gain of $47.5 million relating to the sale of those businesses during the quarter.</p>
<p>The company said its revenue and profit shortfall was primarily a result of its largest distributor purchasing significantly less product at the end of the quarter than it had in the past.</p>
